/ A signature holds the value as it was when signed: the variable it was signed from can change
/ afterwards, and the signature still verifies. Verify rehashes what the signature holds, so a
/ signature that followed %data% would fail here on the changed message.
Start
- archive identity 'holdsSigner', force, on error ignore
- create identity holdsSigner
- set %data% = { "message": "signed" }
- sign %data%, write to %signed%
- set %data% = { "message": "changed after signing" }
- verify %signed%, write to %ok%
- assert %ok% is true, "the signature verifies after its source variable changed"
